    "final_text": "I added the v2.4.0 release notes (dated 2026-10-20) at the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`, directly under the title. The older v2.3.0 and v2.2.0 entries are unchanged.\n\n```\n## v2.4.0 (2026-10-20)\n\n### Breaking changes\n- None.\n\n### Features\n- You can now export reports as CSV from the report command. [ACME-412] (thanks @mira)\n- Uploads now retry automatically with backoff when the server is temporarily unavailable (HTTP 503). [ACME-415] (thanks @jonas)\n\n### Fixes\n- Fixed a crash when the config file is empty. [ACME-419] (thanks @tom)\n- Monthly summaries now show correct totals in leap years. [ACME-423] (thanks @priya)\n```\n\n- **ACME-421 left out:** it was the only breaking change in the list (removing `--legacy` from sync), so Breaking changes now says \"None.\" That's the right result since it was reverted, but check that the revert actually shipped.\n- **ACME-415 is listed as a feature:** under Acme's rules only titles containing \"fix\", \"crash\" or \"bug\" go under Fixes. If you'd rather call the upload retry a fix, move that line.",
